            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0179" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v01/pg147"/>

                <head>74. Telegram From the Director of the Office of Philippine and Southeast Asian
                    Affairs (Young) to the Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d74-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-03-25T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 25,
                                1955—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4116. Prime Minister Faure at lunch
                    yesterday stressed following points to Achilles and me as regards Franco-American relations IC and emphasized he, La
                        Forest and members his government intend work for these
                    objectives: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Policy French Government to work 100 percent with US in IC and considers closest Franco-American
                            cooperation IC not only important IC states but essential to Free
                            World.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>French Government will not play “double game” in Vietnam, i.e. follow
                            one policy in North Vietnam and another in South. Faure stressed French effort directed
                            toward building up South. He said he intends maintain Sainteny as French delegate general
                            North Vietnam in view Sainteny’s
                            entree with Viet Minh leaders; however, Faure opposed to any political
                            arrangements with Viet Minh as well as <pb
                                facs="0180" n="148" xml:id="pg148"/> French Government participation
                            in proposed Franco-Viet Minh mixed
                            companies.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Faure underlined, on other hand, that US
                    must endeavor understand French Parliamentary sensitivity on subject IC and must appreciate position French Government
                    this regard.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#bold">[</hi><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Young</hi></signed><hi
                        rendition="#bold">]</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
